[Aspect ratio 32:9 (fan patch)]
author=Mord of Swoonlight (after Arapapa's Widescreen 16:9)
description=Widescreen view for 32:9 screens: the 3-D view shows more at the left and right, with nothing stretched or cropped (the "Hor+" kind of widescreen). The health and spirit gauges keep their shape at the screen edges; the center ring, help bar, notices, dialogue, use-item popups and weapon name keep their shape too, and menus, documents and the title, save and Options screens keep theirs in the middle of the screen. Pick ONE aspect ratio, and don't combine it with Widescreen 16:9. Set PCSX2's aspect ratio to Fit to Window (game Properties -> Graphics -> Display) and play fullscreen. Takes effect at boot.
// k = 0.3750: x-scale 0.375, clip width 1704, culling width x5.34375; 2-D HUD code in 0x2AF5D8..0x2AFED8 (scripts/aspect_hud.py)
// Guarded: applies only over the original values; a second aspect group does nothing.
